## What advances each objective

In a `--compose` build, SEAM 8 subscribes this tracker to the project's own
gameplay events, so progress is reported without you writing any glue:

| Type | Advanced by |
|---|---|
| `reach` | the scene trigger's `OnActivated` |
| `collect`, `interact` | the world interactable's `OnInteract` |
| `eliminate` | the enemy spawner's `OnDespawned` (one per instance leaving play) |
| `survive` | this component's own clock — one count per second |
| `escort` | nothing: no honest signal exists yet, so it is left unwired and named in the build log |

A single source binds a single objective: two `eliminate` objectives sharing one
spawner would both advance on every kill, so only the first is wired and the rest
are reported at build time rather than mis-wired.

Standalone (no `--compose`), call `ReportProgress(objectiveId, amount)` yourself.
`story_beat_ref` from the authored `MissionSpec` is still passed through as
metadata only. `MissionSpec.triggers` becomes `SendMessage` action names on the
composed trigger zone, which your own scripts can implement by name.
